 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 511346,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "True or False. The slope of the line containing the points (1, 2) and (2, 4) is 1.",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1000618,
     "content_html": "True",
     "correctness": "0.0"
    },
    {
     "id": 1000619,
     "content_html": "False",
     "correctness": "1.0"
    }
   ],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "true-false"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The slope is 2, not 1.</p>\n<p>Point 1: (1, 2) and Point 2: (2, 4).</p>\n<p>Find the slope.</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered unstyled\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"m = \\frac{{{y_2} - {y_1}}}{{{x_2} - {x_1}}} = \\frac{{4 - 2}}{{2 - 1}}\"></span></td>\n<td>Substitute.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"m = \\frac{2}{1} = 2\"></span></td>\n<td>Simplify.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>The slope is 2.</p>\n<p>You can plot the points and verify the slope by counting the rise over the run.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "False"
    }
   ],
